@clawsweeper re-review

The new head fixes CI fixtures without changing production behavior: release spies forward authority, history patches assert the physical client, scoped request failures preserve cause identity, and the native-process fixture acknowledges interrupts before emitting their matching terminal. Its three formerly timed-out cases now pass; independent P2 review is clean. Broader Testbox proof is in progress.

Maintainer resolution of the earlier generic compatibility/data-model flags: the earlier review’s complete paginated 143-file scope matched its local diff; this head adds four test/support files. This change adds no config, environment, schema version, migration, or protocol surface. The compatibility registry records retained released SDK signatures; it is not a database migration. The predecessor field already exists. Released SDK checks pass, and reversible deletion precommit veto/rollback remains covered.

